+# eye(studio): human-eye QA cycle II — 2026-10-28 — tablet (768 px) sweep, mirror parity, auth-failure deploy specificity. Three new evidence dimensions, zero duplicates of #1783/#1799/#1797.
+
+Human-eye role cycle (2026-10-28 07:20+08 dispatch, Job 478330). Complements the three prior studio-QA evidence sets rather than re-treading them: #1783 (landing FCP + tap targets at 390 px), #1799 (F-1…F-6: login breakage, chat leak, contrast, mobile clip at 375 px), and #1797 (cold-FCP distribution 208–1220 ms + first LCP/CLS report). This cycle covers the dimensions none of them touched: **tablet-class viewport (768×1024)**, **deploy-mirror parity** (`supremeai-studio.pages.dev` vs `supremeai-studio.vercel.app`), and **auth-failure deploy specificity** (a new datum sharpening #1799's F-1). **Report-only** — no code changed.
+
+**Target:** `https://supremeai-studio.pages.dev` (primary) and `https://supremeai-studio.vercel.app` (mirror).
+**Probe window:** 2026-10-27 23:20–23:40 UTC (2026-10-28 07:20–07:40 +08).
+**Conditions (no synthetic claims):** agent-browser headless Chrome; isolated fresh sessions for cold-cache samples; 1280×720 / 768×1024 / default emulated viewports; network **unthrottled**; **no Lighthouse/Web Vitals score claimed**; zero-credential throughout. MCP Control Tower handshake 21/21 services healthy at cycle start.
+
+## 1. Corroborating datum: cold-cache FCP re-measured independently (mandate PASS holds)
+
+#1797's pass-2 reported a cold-FCP distribution of 208–1220 ms with a variance caveat. This cycle re-measured independently with isolated fresh browser sessions (guaranteed cold cache, no shared storage) and got **332 / 608 / 420 ms (median 420 ms)** over three navigations of `/` on the Pages host — every sample inside the <1.0 s mandate bar, consistent with #1797's distribution. Navigation transfer size 2.6 KB HTML shell; TTFB sampled at the edge five times via curl: **47–88 ms**; the Vercel mirror measured **520 ms cold FCP / 47 ms TTFB** — same application (identical document title), inside the bar on both deploys. The independent re-measurement strengthens the pass verdict: the funnel is fast for a first-visit user on both hosts under the stated conditions.
+
+## 2. NEW dimension A — tablet 768×1024 sweep (first tablet-class evidence in the series)
+
+Prior cycles tested 1280 px (desktop) and 375/390 px (mobile); no tablet-class evidence existed.
+
+| Check @768×1024 | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Horizontal overflow (`/`, `/chat`, `/login`, `/about`) | **PASS** — `scrollWidth == clientWidth == 768` on all four routes |
+| Navigation layout at 768 | Desktop navbar persists (hamburger hidden, nav links inline); no mobile-menu regression at the breakpoint boundary |
+| Primary CTA tap targets | "Try Live Guest Chat" **210×48 px**, "Create Free Account" **209×50 px** — PASS |
+| Sign In button | 72×32 px — above the WCAG 2.5.8 24 px minimum, below the 44 px comfort convention |
+| Nav links (Features/Live Demo/Our Story) | **58–70 px wide × 20 px tall, zero padding, at both 768 and 1280** — see analysis below |
+| `/chat` model selector | **NOT clipped at 768**: `select.flex-1` renders 539 px wide, right edge 735 < 768 — confirms #1799's F-4 is specific to the 375 px class |
+| Console / page errors | Zero errors; only benign `[PWA] Service Worker registered` + heartbeat warnings (matches #1799) |
+
+**Nav-link target size — measured, not assumed.** The inline nav links measure 20 px tall, under the WCAG 2.2 §2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) AA bar of 24×24 CSS px. However the §2.5.8 **spacing exception** is satisfied on measurement: a 24 px-diameter circle centered on each target does not intersect any adjacent target's circle (Features↔Live Demo center distance 88 px ≫ 24 px; single header row means no vertical neighbors; computed padding 0/0 confirms the bounding boxes are the true hit areas). **Verdict: PASS, not a defect.** Recorded as a comfort-target improvement opportunity (padding-only fix, e.g. `py-2 -my-2`) for any future nav touch — deliberately NOT filed as an issue to keep the finding register honest. Same result at 1280 px.
+
+## 3. NEW dimension B — deploy-mirror parity
+
+Both hosts are referenced in-repo (`src/utils/portalHosts.test.ts`) but prior cycles probed them separately for different things (#1783 → Vercel perf; #1799 → Pages journeys). Cross-host parity this cycle: same document title and application shell; cold FCP 520 ms (Vercel) vs 332–608 ms (Pages); edge TTFB 47 ms vs 47–88 ms; security headers present on both (HSTS + CSP with identical directives observed). **No parity drift detected at the funnel level.**
+
+## 4. NEW dimension C — auth-failure deploy specificity (sharpens #1799's F-1)
+
+#1799's F-1 (CRITICAL: sign-in broken on the Pages deploy) observed `POST /api/auth/passkey/login/options → 405` and hypothesized a base-URL/configuration mismatch (auth calls go same-origin to the static host while working API calls go to the Render gateway). This cycle's cross-host probe adds a discriminating datum:
+
+| Probe (fresh, no credentials) | pages.dev | vercel.app |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/auth/passkey/login/options` | **HTTP 405** (0 B body) | **HTTP 404** (22 B body) |
+
+Both hosts fail, **differently**: the static-CDN 405 (method not allowed — path served, POST refused) vs Vercel's outright 404 (no route at all). The failure mode is CDN-specific but the defect is **app-level**: the auth client targets the static origin on both deploys, and neither static host has any auth server surface. This strengthens F-1's proposed fix path (point the auth client at the API gateway origin, as the working `/api/config/*` calls already do) and rules out a Pages-only misconfiguration. Not re-filed — it is evidence for #1799's F-1, recorded here for the fixer lane; no issue-comment tool exists on the tower, so this report is the evidence carrier.
+
