+
+- **#1783** — landing FCP/vendor-chunks/390 px scroll: no overlap with tablet sweep, mirror parity, or auth datum.
+- **#1799** — F-1…F-6 at 375 px + journeys: F-4 re-confirmed as 375 px-specific (bounds narrowed, not duplicated); F-1 sharpened with new cross-host datum, not re-filed; no other overlap.
+- **#1797** — cold-FCP distribution + LCP/CLS: my cold-FCP samples are **corroboration** (Section 1, labeled as such); no LCP/CLS re-measurement attempted; tablet/mirror/auth dimensions are new.
+- Queue sweep of 20 open work orders against `login/passkey/auth/405/404/contrast/wcag/leak/clip/selector/eye/funnel/fcp/tap/studio`: no unclaimed issue covers the three new dimensions.
+
+## 6. Never-do register
+
+- Report-only: no runtime code, config, or workflow changed; production probed read-only, no redeploys triggered.
+- No Lighthouse/Web Vitals scores claimed; all numbers are dated, conditioned, and method-labeled.
+- No credentials, tokens, or tenant data used; zero-credential session end to end.
+- No issue filed for the 20 px nav links: the WCAG spacing exception applies on measurement — filing it would pollute the defect register with a non-defect.
+
+**Verdict: funnel performance mandate PASSES on re-measurement (cold, both hosts); tablet class PASSES with the F-4 defect bounded to 375 px; mirror parity holds; one new discriminating datum for the open CRITICAL F-1. Zero new defects, zero duplicates.**
